.nh
.TH "BCDOCK" "1" "Jan 2025" "BCDock CLI" "BCDock Manual"

.SH NAME
bcdock-me-export-latest - Show your most recent data export, and download it if it is ready


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbcdock me export latest [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show your most recent data export in any state (pending, ready, failed or
expired), with its download link when ready. With --out, download it, without
starting a new export the way 'bcdock me export' does.

.PP
Auth: any API key scope; it reads only your own export.

.PP
Exit codes:
  0   ok (including "no export yet")
  1   general error (--out on an export that is not ready)
  3   auth failure (missing or invalid token)
  4   rate-limited


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for latest

.PP
\fB--out\fP=""
	Download the latest export to this path (it must be ready)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	API base URL (env: BCDOCK_API_URL)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable colored output

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="table"
	Output format: table, json, csv

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-essential output

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30s
	Request timeout

.PP
\fB--token\fP=""
	API token (env: BCDOCK_TOKEN)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  bcdock me export latest
  bcdock me export latest --out export.zip
  bcdock me export latest -o json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBbcdock-me-export(1)\fP
